{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0122V2gXzbn4F8DbafdXFwX8","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→import { NextResponse, type NextRequest } from \"next/server\";\n     2→import { createClient } from \"@supabase/supabase-js\";\n     3→\n     4→export async function GET(request: NextRequest) {\n     5→  const requestUrl = new URL(request.url);\n     6→  const code = requestUrl.searchParams.get(\"code\");\n     7→  const origin = requestUrl.origin;\n     8→\n     9→  // Create a fresh Supabase client for server-side operations\n    10→  const supabaseUrl = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL;\n    11→  const supabaseAnonKey = process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY;\n    12→\n    13→  if (!supabaseUrl || !supabaseAnonKey) {\n    14→    console.error(\"Missing Supabase environment variables\");\n    15→    return NextResponse.redirect(`${origin}/es?error=config_error`);\n    16→  }\n    17→\n    18→  const supabase = createClient(supabaseUrl, supabaseAnonKey);\n    19→\n    20→  if (code) {\n    21→    const { data: sessionData, error } = await supabase.auth.exchangeCodeForSession(code);\n    22→    if (error) {\n    23→      console.error(\"Auth callback error:\", error);\n    24→      return NextResponse.redirect(`${origin}/es?error=auth_callback_failed`);\n    25→    }\n    26→\n    27→    // Check if the user has a profile with a username (full_name)\n    28→    if (sessionData?.user) {\n    29→      const { data: profile } = await supabase\n    30→        .from(\"profiles\")\n    31→        .select(\"full_name\")\n    32→        .eq(\"id\", sessionData.user.id)\n    33→        .maybeSingle();\n    34→\n    35→      // If no profile or no username, redirect to complete profile page\n    36→      if (!profile?.full_name) {\n    37→        return NextResponse.redirect(`${origin}/es/complete-profile`);\n    38→      }\n    39→    }\n    40→  }\n    41→\n    42→  // Redirect to the default locale home page after successful verification\n    43→  return NextResponse.redirect(`${origin}/es`);\n    44→}\n    45→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KtuiUVNNMHPKNssgRXtHCS","session_id":"dd558466-241e-4005-8014-18e5732e4b3e","uuid":"e33619f2-26b4-4225-9ef6-252157ce3a06"}
